### Run with: dotnet run --project src/Orders  (http profile: port 44050)
@host = http://localhost:44050

### 1. Regular order -> the consumer processes it and publishes OrderProcessed (only "all-orders" gets it)
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customer": "ana", "product": "book", "amount": 50 }

### 2. Large order -> BOTH subscriptions get it ("high-value" filters amount > 1000)
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customer": "bruno", "product": "laptop", "amount": 2500 }

### 3. Duplicate detection: send it TWICE in a row with the same id -> the broker drops the second one
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111", "customer": "carla", "product": "pen", "amount": 5 }

### 4. Invalid order -> explicit dead-letter with a reason, no retries
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customer": "dani", "product": "mouse", "amount": 0 }

### 5. Transient failure -> 3 attempts (MaxDeliveryCount), then it lands in the DLQ on its own
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customer": "eli", "product": "flaky", "amount": 30 }

### 6. Look at the DLQ (peek, does not consume)
GET {{host}}/dlq

### 7. Replay the DLQ (the "flaky" one now succeeds; the invalid one goes back to the DLQ)
POST {{host}}/dlq/replay
